{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQLFp2j7khHBUqdmp6bY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the missing tests for both blocking findings and wrote the report. Only a subset of plan.md's test plan is covered. I changed no production code this round.\n\n`go test ./worker ./reviewfix` and `go vet` on both pass. I did not run `make lint test`, or the committer, gitx and servecmd tests, this round.\n\n- **Worker conflict flow:** the new `internal/worker/conflict_round_test.go` covers these cases:\n  - `conflict.md` has the untrusted header, escaped path names, a path cap, and `mainTip` taken from the remote.\n  - A clean merge gives no input, and a PR with no conflict round is ignored.\n  - `preMerge` fails on a conflict count mismatch and on an unexpected path.\n  - A resolved round: the agent sees real markers, `conflict.md` replaces `review-feedback.md`, and `MergeParent` is the fetched main tip.\n  - Leftover conflict markers hold the job with nothing committed.\n- **Landing check:** `TestMergeIncludesSecondParentOnMain` in `internal/reviewfix/loop_test.go` covers the second parent on main (true), not on main (false), a fetch error, and head equal to base. I extended the stub in `internal/reviewfix/harness_test.go` to support those cases.\n\nI left the hard-coded `main` alone. The committer's `cfg.Branch` is documented as applying to the main-branch committer only, so for worker code the committer also uses `main`. The worker opens its PRs against `main` too.\n\nNot done, and listed in the report's open issues:\n- The servecmd `Rounds` wiring test, the end-to-end test and the prgate whitespace case, which the reviewer marked non-blocking.\n- Several plan.md tests: the diff guard counting only the PR's own changes, no git running in the agent's tree, and rejection of a workflow change.\n- Tests for `conflict.md`'s backtick fence, redaction and UTF-8 truncation. `conflict.md` currently lists paths only, with no hunks, so there is nothing to test yet.\n\nThe report is `.ard/323/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1021,"cache_read_input_tokens":56910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1021},"output_tokens":708,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45683568-b4ae-4291-a5dd-649010da8346","uuid":"fbe3af25-fac6-4338-9e86-98b916e70464","timestamp":"2026-11-25T21:10:35.734Z","request_id":"req_011ChQLFouHZ53j9KSdb5TNJ"}
